        "original_id": "ea4c777a-dc36-53f0-ac28-240a2ac863f5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Leeds, Yorkshire's West Riding, West Yorkshire, England\n- Organizations: Kingdom of Elmet, Elmet\n- Products: St John's Centre\n\nFacts:\n- In the 5th century, the name Leeds referred to a wooded area of the Kingdom of Elmet.\n- Elmet was an independent Brittonic kingdom from about the 5th century to the early 7th century.\n- Elmet was located in an area that later became the West Riding of Yorkshire.\n- Leeds was historically in Yorkshire's West Riding.\n- St John's Centre is an indoor shopping centre in Leeds, West Yorkshire, England.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
